        <item>
            <title>1.5.17</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 17:57:14 +0900</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>49</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.5.17</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Added</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Pasted files are selected after a paste, like Windows Explorer.</b> After ⌘V finishes, the pasted file(s) become the selection and scroll into view — instant proof the paste landed, even when you pasted while another file's row was highlighted. Works for copy and cut pastes, uses the final names (so a conflict resolved as "keep both" selects "file 2.txt"), and only applies to items that landed in the folder you're viewing.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li>Undo-restore now reselects restored items in icon views too (previously the reselection only worked in List/Details).</li>
<li>Reselection after refresh no longer misses folders or files whose names differ only in Unicode composition (Korean names on SMB shares).</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
